\ prog/udpecho.fam — the UDP echo server as a program: it holds port 3737 and
\ answers every datagram with itself.  What prog/udpsrv.fam did inside the
\ kernel, now in user mode: the frames reach it through its ring, the answers
\ leave as requests.  Built with lib/pnet.fam, src/eth.fam, src/ip.fam,
\ src/udp.fam and lib/pstack.fam (scripts/build.sh).
: esk variable ;  : ebuf variable ;
400 lit pstack
E99 lit udpbind esk !  600 lit alloc ebuf !
11 lit E99 lit pbind ?dup if "udpecho: cannot hold port 3737: " puts u. '\n' lit putc texit then
"udpecho: serving UDP port 3737\n" puts
begin
	nbit 0 lit wait drop
	begin netrx while pnetin netrel
		begin esk @ ebuf @ 600 lit udprecv dup 0< 0= while
			udpfrom esk @ -rot ebuf @ 4 lit pick udpsend drop drop
		repeat drop
	repeat
0 lit until
